.TH BTK-ADDRESS 1 "15 August 2026" "Bitcoin Toolkit 4.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
btk-address \- derive P2PKH, P2WPKH, or BIP-341 P2TR addresses
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B btk address
[\fB\-\-type\fR \fIp2pkh\fR|\fIp2wpkh\fR|\fIp2tr\fR]...
[\fB\-\-match\fR \fIREGEX\fR]
[\fB\-\-ignore-case\fR]
[\fB\-\-network\fR \fImainnet\fR|\fItestnet\fR]
[\fB\-\-source\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Derive a Bitcoin address from an explicit private or public key. Items are
read from stdin. There are no positional key arguments.
.PP
Each stdin item is a typed
.B privkey
or
.B pubkey
object, or a bare line determined in this order: WIF, then a 66- or
130-character hex public key. There is no
.BR \-\-from .
64-character hex, decimal, leftover text, and binary stdin are
.BR "not a private or public key" .
A WIF-shaped string with a bad checksum is
.BR "invalid WIF checksum" .
.PP
Default
.B \-\-type
is one
.BR p2wpkh .
The flag is repeatable; addresses are emitted in flag order.
.B p2wpkh
and
.B p2tr
require a compressed key.
.B p2tr
is BIP-341 key-path with an empty script tree (tweaked), encoded as
bech32m witness v1. There is no
.B \-\-bech32m
flag.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show this help and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-type " p2pkh|p2wpkh|p2tr"
Address script to produce. Repeatable. Default
.BR p2wpkh .
Unknown values are
.BR "unknown address type" .
.TP
.BI \-\-match " REGEX"
POSIX extended regular expression on the address
.BR data .
Non-matches are dropped. Empty stdout is still exit 0. May be passed
once. Invalid patterns are
.BR "invalid match pattern" .
Implies
.BR \-\-source .
.TP
.B \-\-ignore-case
Add
.B REG_ICASE
to
.BR \-\-match .
.TP
.B \-\-source
Include the input item as a
.B source
object even without
.BR \-\-match .
A typed object is copied as received, including a nested
.B source
if present. On a bare string the source is synthesized (WIF private key or hex
public key); the
.B data
field is the bare input.
.TP
.BI \-\-network " mainnet|testnet"
Network for hex public keys and typed objects that omit
.BR network .
WIF version bytes take precedence. A typed object's
.B network
field takes precedence over this flag. Default mainnet. Does not walk
.BR source .
.TP
.BI \-\-out " ndjson|json|plain"
Output framing. Default ndjson.
.TP
.BI \-\-in " auto|ndjson|json|plain"
Stdin framing. Default auto.
.SH NOTES
64-hex is never treated as an x-only internal key. Feed a secret hex or
decimal value as a typed
.B privkey
object
.RI ( "btk privkey --from hex | btk address" ).
.PP
Vanity search is a pipe:
.PP
.nf
btk privkey --new --stream | btk address --type p2pkh --match '^1bri'
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR btk (1),
.BR btk-privkey (1),
.BR btk-pubkey (1)
